{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba web/design-system/tokens.css | head -75'","aggregated_output":"     1\t/* Shared Hivemind theme tokens. */\n     2\t:root {\n     3\t  --paper: #f5f2eb;\n     4\t  --wash: #ebe9e2;\n     5\t  --wash-strong: #e3e0d9;\n     6\t  --rule: #dfddd6;\n     7\t  --rule-strong: #c9c7c0;\n     8\t  --ink: #0f140d;\n     9\t  --ink-2: #393d36;\n    10\t  --ink-3: #6a6c65;\n    11\t  --ink-4: #9f9f98;\n    12\t  --scrim: rgba(245, 242, 235, 0.72);\n    13\t  --shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(15, 20, 13, 0.04), 0 12px 32px rgba(15, 20, 13, 0.10);\n    14\t\n    15\t  --sans: \"Geist\", \"Helvetica Neue\", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\n    16\t  --mono: \"Geist Mono\", \"SF Mono\", Menlo, Consolas, monospace;\n    17\t\n    18\t  --gutter: 40px;\n    19\t  --control-height: 30px;\n    20\t  --ease: cubic-bezier(0.2, 0, 0, 1);\n    21\t  color-scheme: light;\n    22\t}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r76.md | head -40'","aggregated_output":"     1\t**Verdict: not ready to build.** The package check is sound, but the screen check could pass a page that says “1284 pieces of evidence” and shows only one summary. It could also reject a correct page because five genuine source titles contain “Bullish.” [RELEASE-PAGE.md:134](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:134) · [RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:145](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:145)\n     2\t\n     3\t1. **An ordinary source link breaks the zero-request promise.** I counted 1,258 HTTP(S) source entries under `old-1/v8`. Clicking one can navigate from the local file to the publisher. `noopener noreferrer` suppresses opener and referrer information. It still permits navigation. Opening `<details>` itself needs no request. For the promise written in §0, render the source address as plain text and check that expanding the evidence creates no navigable links. The `file://` test can then run with Chrome’s normal file restrictions. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:16](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:16) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:64](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:64) · [CSP navigation directives](https://www.w3.org/TR/CSP3/#directives-navigation)\n     4\t\n     5\t2. **The specified JSON escaping leaves the closing tag intact.** I checked the file bytes. Line 38 gives the same literal characters on both sides of “escaped as.” A source containing `</script>` can therefore end the data block before the page script reads it. Specify the literal JSON escape sequences `\\u003c`, `\\u003e`, `\\u0026`, `\\u2028` and `\\u2029`. Declare UTF-8 at the start of the file and put the CSP before the style, script and embedded data. Test the existing fixture in the browser with its evidence expanded. Its exact quote must be visible as text, with no image element created. The proposed “no second `<script>` start” check misses the closing tag, and parsing JSON alone never exercises the proposed `innerHTML` mutant. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:37](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:37) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:104](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:104) · [HTML script parsing](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/scripting.html#restrictions-for-contents-of-script-elements) · [CSP meta placement](https://www.w3.org/TR/CSP3/#meta-element)\n     6\t\n     7\t3. **Keep byte-for-byte rendering and format 2. Update the checks that depend on format 1.** Read all three files once through the open directory handle. Hash and compare those same page bytes against `render_page(raw_data)` using the same data bytes that passed the store check. That certifies the inspected copy. Adding a required file and manifest member justifies `/2` while the data allow-list stays `/1`. The existing acceptance script pins `/1`, and two helpers that deliberately alter data refresh only the data hash. Their format-2 copies must also regenerate the page and its hash so the forged forecast still reaches the store comparison. Add the converse case too: a correct page with only `page_sha256` wrong must fail for that exact reason. Every proposed page-tampering test refreshes that hash, so deleting the hash check currently escapes them. [release.py:454](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:454) · [release_check.py:24](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:24) · [release_check.py:128](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:128) · [test_release.py:180](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:180) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:109](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:109)\n     8\t\n     9\t4. **Check what the reader sees both before and after expanding `v8`.** Pin the exact question, “How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?”, alongside the three stated labels. For the expanded card, freeze the expected ordered evidence and source values from the accepted package before the run. Compare the displayed entries with that expectation, including the full Morningstar quote and attribution. This catches missing, duplicated or misplaced entries and permits “Bullish” exactly where the source used it. Close and reopen the card once to catch a second copy being appended. Apply the same discipline to the two dated cards: pin the day and question, require “Answer: Yes,” expand their evidence, and check the known explanation phrases there too. A collapsed page-text search cannot inspect content the script has yet to create. [FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:134](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:134) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:69](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:69) · [release_check.py:173](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:173) · [RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:60](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:60)\n    10\t\n    11\t5. **Credit the fetch test only when Chrome identifies the attempted connection.** The Chrome 158 probe recorded in the design answers the CDP question for this Mac: the blocked fetch produced two log errors and zero `Network.requestWillBeSent` events. Recompute the altered inline script’s CSP hash so the test script actually runs. Require the normal card to render and the security event to name the intended destination and `connect-src`. A stale script hash would otherwise earn credit for blocking the whole script. Port 9 also has an independent browser block, so a generic fetch error there proves too little. Enable observation before navigation and keep it active through expansion. If “zero console errors” remains a condition, include `Runtime.consoleAPICalled` for `console.error`. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:130](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:130) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:144](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:144) · [Fetch port blocking](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#port-blocking) · [CDP console events](https://chromedevtools.github.io/devtools-protocol/tot/Runtime/#event-consoleAPICalled)\n    12\t\n    13\t6. **Correct two browser acceptance conditions.** A blocked inline script leaves browser scripting enabled, so `<noscript>` stays hidden. If the reader should see a fallback in that case, put ordinary visible text in the page and replace it after successful rendering. The 3-second and size budgets **are** set before the first screen control. Start the timer at navigation and stop when the full expected list is visible. Starting at `load` can omit the work of parsing and rendering the embedded data. The state table also promises a phone-width and dark-scheme check that §6 never performs. Either define its viewport and observable pass condition or remove the acceptance claim. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:79](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:79) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:155](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:155) · [HTML `noscript` behavior](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/scripting.html#the-noscript-element)\n    14\t\n    15\tThe separate release page fits D758 and requires no POC change. The text filter is optional for D756. I would leave it out of this slice so acceptance covers the reader’s actual task: opening a question and seeing all its sources with the forecast withheld. This was a read-only review. The Chrome observation above comes from the probe recorded in the design. [D756:11833](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11833) · [D758:11881](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11881) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:59](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:59)","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'FORMAT|package files|hash|read once' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md | tail -14\"","aggregated_output":"11:  `fstat`). It hashes and parses the same bytes and returns `(counts, data, bytes)`, so the command reports what was checked.\n18:  - package files are opened without waiting (`O_NONBLOCK`), so a named pipe is refused by type instead of blocking `check` (test 15);\n116:  - `FORMAT = 'hivemind-release/1'`;\n366:   - an extra manifest key with an unchanged data hash fails;\n386:    copy of the package with that same source removed and its manifest hash refreshed. `check` refuses, naming the missing item. (An\n413:    - a data file whose repeated `one_line` member has the genuine value last, with the manifest hash refreshed so every other\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r76c.md | head -60 && nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r76e.md | head -35'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r76c.md | head -60 && nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r76e.md | head -35'","aggregated_output":"     1\t**Not ready to build.** Revision 3 catches the extra forecast line from round 76b when it appears inside the `v8` card. Put the same line immediately above the card and the reader still sees “Forecast: $361 billion,” while every card comparison passes. D756 requires checking what appears on the reader’s screen. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:187](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:187) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:207](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:207) · [DECISIONS-log.md:11835](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11835)\n     2\t\n     3\t| Round‑76b finding | Revision‑3 assessment |\n     4\t|---|---|\n     5\t| 1. Source links | **Closed.** Addresses appear as plain text. The expanded page must contain zero links, `href` attributes, or `src` attributes. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:91](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:91) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:198](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:198) |\n     6\t| 2. Embedded JSON | **Closed.** The design specifies the literal escapes and header order. The browser must display the exact fixture quote with no image element. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:57](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:57) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:210](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:210) |\n     7\t| 3. Format 2 and package checks | **Closed.** The checker compares and hashes the same page bytes. A correct page with only its recorded hash wrong must fail. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:73](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:73) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:143](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:143) |\n     8\t| 4. What the cards show | **Partly closed.** The `v8` comparison preserves all 1,284 evidence groups and their order. The dated-package correction is closed. I verified that August 25 `old-3/v36` asks about Rubin Ultra and August 28 `old-1/v10` asks about Firmus. Each has “Yes,” one evidence entry, and one source. The screen comparison still has the gap described below. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:174](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:174) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:193](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:193) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:201](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:201) |\n     9\t| 5. Blocked fetch | **Closed.** Observation begins before navigation. The altered script must render the list, and Chrome’s security error must identify both the destination and `connect-src`. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:167](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:167) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:213](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:213) |\n    10\t| 6. Browser acceptance conditions | **Partly closed.** The fallback, phone width, and literal dark and light colours are specified. The timer can still stop while the list is invisible. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:49](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:49) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:226](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:226) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:232](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:232) |\n    11\t\n    12\t**Two corrections are needed before build.**\n    13\t\n    14\t1. **Check the complete screen, including the text around the selected card.** Freeze the expected header and collapsed question list, then compare the page again with the selected card expanded. Keep the existing evidence grouping. Require the extra-line test to fail when the line is a sibling of `v8`. The card’s text-node walk also misses words drawn by CSS `::before` or `::after`. For this fixed template, requiring all reader-facing words to come from text nodes and checking that its stylesheet generates no text closes that gap. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:84](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:84) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:187](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:187) · [W3C generated-content specification](https://www.w3.org/TR/css-pseudo-4/#generated-content)\n    15\t\n    16\t2. **Use the same visibility test for the evidence and the three-second timer.** A list with `opacity: 0` still has non-zero boxes. Its text passes the stated card-reading conditions, and removing the fallback satisfies the timer’s other condition. Check visibility through ancestors, including zero opacity, and require every expected question before stopping the timer. A copy with the list fully transparent should miss the deadline even though all its cards exist. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:187](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:187) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:232](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:232) · [CSSOM visibility algorithm](https://drafts.csswg.org/cssom-view/#dom-element-checkvisibility)\n    17\t\n    18\tI found no additional request path or implementation blocker in the specified page. This was a read-only design review. Slice 2 has no implementation yet, so its browser behavior remains unverified. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:3](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:3)     1\t**Not ready to build from the available design.** I read `RELEASE-PAGE.md` end to end. Its status still says “revision 4, for council round 76d,” and its phone-width check still allows the reader to miss Morningstar’s $361 billion estimate. I could not verify revision 5. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:3](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:3) · [release_check.py:175](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:175)\n     2\t\n     3\t1. **The two earlier fixes remain closed.** An extra forecast beside a card must fail the whole-page comparison. A fully transparent question list must miss the three-second deadline. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:200](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:200) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:226](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:226) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:252](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:252)\n     4\t2. **The one serious 76d finding remains open in this file.** A quote clipped to its first line still has a visible box. The check then reads the entire underlying text, and the phone-width check can pass because clipping creates no horizontal scroll. I found no separate forecast leak, outgoing request path, or build blocker in the available design. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:197](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:197) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:247](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:247)\n     5\t3. **Revision 5 is needed for sign-off.** The decisive test is the one 76d requested. At 390 px, expand `v8` and scroll to Morningstar’s quote. The full quote must be readable, and an otherwise identical copy clipped to one line must fail. [codex-r76d.md:10](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r76d.md:10)","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
