{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"web_search","id":"exec-f4e7fb96-a912-4c78-b850-afa29ff64556","query":"'The contents of the element including any ink'","action":{"type":"find_in_page","pattern":"The contents of the element including any ink"},"results":[{"type":"text_result","domain":"www.w3.org","ref_id":"turn1view0","snippet":"Total lines: 1350","title":"CSS Containment Module Level 2","url":"https://www.w3.org/TR/css-contain-2/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"www.w3.org","ref_id":"turn1view1","snippet":"Total lines: 2849","title":"CSSOM View Module","url":"https://www.w3.org/TR/cssom-view-1/"}]}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"agent_message","text":"**Not ready to build.** Revision 5 catches a quote shortened with an ellipsis, but the screen check can still pass when the reader cannot see Morningstar’s $361 billion estimate. I found one other false pass in dark mode. The design identifies itself as revision 5 and has no implementation yet. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:3](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:3)\n\n1. **The 76d clipping finding is partly closed.** The new test catches clipping applied directly to the quote. The remaining gap is at line 209, where the check measures only the element holding the text. A one-line wrapper with `contain: paint` can hide everything after the first line while the quote inside still wraps normally. Its dimensions, line count and position within the phone viewport can all pass. The `$361 billion` estimate comes late in the stored quote. Require the quote’s line rectangles to fit inside any ancestor that clips them, and use that one-line wrapper as the failing copy. The two earlier findings carried forward by 76d remain closed: an extra forecast beside the card fails the whole-page comparison, and a transparent list misses the deadline. [codex-r76d.md:10](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r76d.md:10) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:209](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:209) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:237](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:237) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:263](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:263) · [release_check.py:175](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:175) · [W3C paint-containment rule](https://www.w3.org/TR/css-contain-2/#paint-containment)\n\n2. **Dark mode can pass with “Forecast unavailable” invisible.** The dark-mode assertion checks only the body background. If the marker keeps the same `--ink` colour as the background behind it, its text, dimensions and opacity all pass while the reader sees a blank space. Specify the marker’s readable foreground and background together. A dark page that draws both in `--ink` should fail. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:206](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:206) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:265](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:265) · [tokens.css:8](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/web/design-system/tokens.css:8) · [W3C visibility check](https://www.w3.org/TR/cssom-view-1/#dom-element-checkvisibility)\n\nI found no separate forecast leak, outgoing request path or ambiguity that prevents implementation. Both blockers concern what the screen check can certify. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:70](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:70) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:89](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:89) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:185](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:185)"}}
